m "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-3,1),(-2,-1),$ and $(4,-4).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi y}{2}\\,j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-3,1) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (-3))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (1)}{2})\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(-2,-1) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (-2))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-1)}{2})\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(4,-4) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi (4))\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (-4)}{2})\\,j=2\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/33/33c6c3680f3cab38ffd1508fad160948f3bc1159c01dc287b3fe113c0cf89875.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d9715f6-880f-5e90-9ccb-eb9b334a39ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fc954607d17ae1eadaa0aba8d939343290a5c20f47bf61863cba9c42d9f558c9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253919} {:answer/id #uuid "3b6397c3-941a-58f5-887e-447432631c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254186} {:answer/id #uuid "44afdd8c-abe1-588b-af9c-32a4909426e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/2100cd71f6bbbcc46d3f9f35853f65a9bf0d3f25bf3273db0d244c05221d758d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254251} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb78a7f-9fd3-5fa7-bde9-8571110c7992" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/34/34e44b959282b0bc6c245643329e2b485d3209d89f304cf76c106718120a2f10.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254800} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a32930-3699-5cd6-84b0-329514a970d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0c69bb201b98cd3728527c562bf4e92cef3c48adae4e01725c2497a73c97a0af.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b6397c3-941a-58f5-887e-447432631c73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254186} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f725ff6-094a-5962-a13d-abc513c68fd1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255975}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b3ac067-5818-5125-bedf-bd1f05f196a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122742" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),(1,2),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})\\,i+xy\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-1,1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(-1)(1)\\,j=-3\\,i-j \\\\ F(1,2) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+(1)(2)\\,j=3\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\,i+(2)(-1)\\,j=-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/5e/5e9e75b66969e1acd7b1a90a5243a3a496168644a53d541851ba933a5f465553.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256710 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "423f3338-ffb1-59f0-b120-219b32a13003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/48/4837efc1a78060b2954fa58b26f35e7b2c6d810ce676959653f8e7eca0b5b476.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254234} {:answer/id #uuid "45a53f5e-4056-51ed-a116-9ca60d3c4976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e87092c467b78bfe00651fb9752ed54c7f7784c83612fba2149063eba57952e9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254259} {:answer/id #uuid "71a298d1-6d06-55e3-ab94-8786b46031d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f2/f2835e43d43494d3319a6a0db0a411906f0424bdac8830425bad47723010d95c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254679} {:answer/id #uuid "74a2d6dd-b9fa-5a61-ab75-14dcdad78a4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/68/68d33b11d6476a0d35cb7486073e90e2755b46f1d4f935adc5dafb7087b15b99.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254702} {:answer/id #uuid "dc946e82-d393-53f9-bc76-247d76947cb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc946e82-d393-53f9-bc76-247d76947cb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/58/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255626} :answer-field/id #uuid "832d12ed-0f04-5945-adfb-d9b68890f3c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0ef3069-54df-58ef-8ea9-a7adc99649e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-122744" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=-2x\\,i+{2}^{y}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,2),(-1,1),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=-2x\\,i+{2}^{y}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-4,2) & =-2(-4)\\,i+{2}^{2}\\,j=8\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ F(-1,1) & =-2(-1)\\,i+{2}^{1}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,0) & =-2(2)\\,i+{2}^{0}\\,j=-4\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/58/58a106f2c0ac7aacd30f7ba8915fd2317a67efb73c1c48fe2d192a5d2576717a.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240a8926-bf1a-519e-9693-8f0bba9cbe1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b014bb3efef5caa6a721173a7470f4600edc8207cae6adc3a77bffe217176e13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253993} {:answer/id #uuid "48068bbf-dbb6-513d-a84e-da2cf1e1b829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254278} {:answer/id #uuid "87cdf628-15c5-5fd3-b604-ae4e78fbbb87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/81/81ec06546a0ae47f254f42bfafabcf10c6aa7b776f49c59013c9c198bf1bf89a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254876} {:answer/id #uuid "c7647169-e091-5477-98ce-5a42c5fd0a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e959a73a075acd0e72e4cfa4edd09fa1710c450286ff574574208d42b2d897c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255450} {:answer/id #uuid "fe49859d-ea70-5353-ac0d-504ccb94fae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d1/d150a7172d3a7e876cda685d9b096dd1f8d7d96a3349e355dc26562af75caa47.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48068bbf-dbb6-513d-a84e-da2cf1e1b829" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254278} :answer-field/id #uuid "c344638a-8e0e-5a85-a726-eda285835155" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256266}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5565e07-6be0-586e-b2a1-438c9383fcb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122759" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=-\\frac{x}{y}\\,i-|x|\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-3,1),(2,-1),$ and $(4,2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=-\\frac{x}{y}\\,i-|x|\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-3,1) & =-(\\frac{-3}{1})i-|-3|\\,j=3\\,i-3\\,j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =-(\\frac{2}{-1})i-|2|\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ F(4,2) & =-(\\frac{4}{2})i-|4|\\,j=-2\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/33/330bf1e0b9b2dff008a3e3878d5b2acba8e14addb637d637874492220cb08f2c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380712 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68c8f22e-9c72-5097-9d66-15b73bc21b48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d2/d28dd5c26019ddf8dd9fa1c3034eed957cc5d62e433989d966f34c1623494966.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380714} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb393e8-f46f-59f9-bd05-a8b537c8b025" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b8/b896ff19664a92b34fd8456077b4a91ea2d36121c284001adfbf8216fc49a46c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380715} {:answer/id #uuid "b072cbaa-a0b3-5627-bae1-8d307f2b14e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b96b3f9db529d096b96321e3efe9d645788c763373cfeeaeac559c343215e11a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380716} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6da738-e5c8-5567-b9f8-3a0e4086fc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b0b3eced37ace6c64c65cf94c1621d6706894a079621870b19a69b0f27f2c842.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380717} {:answer/id #uuid "8558fc22-266f-5df8-9ed9-f72208859a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d1/d1fc9c2797e0fa16ba0c6b8f9328680c3706c118d5ed576d09be48e5068537fe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b6da738-e5c8-5567-b9f8-3a0e4086fc28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b0/b0b3eced37ace6c64c65cf94c1621d6706894a079621870b19a69b0f27f2c842.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380717} :answer-field/id #uuid "34658309-80b9-58e6-8164-617fe6aa19b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30d646c9-1021-587c-bc37-6244d8e4d4a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-122764" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{2y}{1-y}\\,i+\\frac{x}{y-1}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,3),(2,-1),$ and $(4,2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=\\frac{2y}{1-y}\\,i+\\frac{x}{y-1}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-2,3) & =\\frac{2(3)}{1-3}\\,i+\\frac{-2}{3-1}\\,j=-3\\,i-j \\\\ F(2,-1) & =\\frac{2(-1)}{1-(-1)}\\,i+\\frac{2}{(-1)-1}\\,j=-i-j \\\\ F(4,2) & =\\frac{2(2)}{1-2}\\,i+\\frac{4}{2-1}\\,j=-4\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/b0/b0b3eced37ace6c64c65cf94c1621d6706894a079621870b19a69b0f27f2c842.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de1513c2-3155-5def-a5b5-5b833a833652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b6/b6a7c1faba2bb5d18d5f729d2576d7475f6ce1784698fae0a1c1ea97b80d6180.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387279} {:answer/id #uuid "f9bf0d9a-d009-5dbb-8f91-ece881c3e02c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d44395fa166c654c41322bd31e1a9bf9bc6c7a398e27da7f9de9d249ccdb1107.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387280} {:answer/id #uuid "0b6544d5-cd56-547b-895e-df2376403680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8c/8cdc92839252560ad52b54bb77d9db75ba066e33bfa5a3c451e4cbb6345e9d33.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387281} {:answer/id #uuid "8bade9cb-3b17-5e2f-ab51-5cbf5f1198f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/25/2560beb4dcff267890c47ad5df8ac7aef0e5de64a57384f8c71e35d8325c892b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387282} {:answer/id #uuid "45a0eeab-6f8a-5b04-8150-613eb8858a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8ec9af02a374c1b8a954117ad055f78e9e2ac74bc391bb230968198a3a474fef.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45a0eeab-6f8a-5b04-8150-613eb8858a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8ec9af02a374c1b8a954117ad055f78e9e2ac74bc391bb230968198a3a474fef.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387283} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc3d49d5-a5f3-575b-83f9-afd438ed4ffd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e446a55-b0d3-59f4-abde-52af19baebe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-122745" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{xy+1}\\,i+\\frac{x}{xy+1}\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,0),(1,-2),$ and $(0,2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=\\frac{y}{xy+1}\\,i+\\frac{x}{xy+1}\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-2,0) & =\\frac{0}{(-2)(0)+1}\\,i+\\frac{-2}{(-2)(0)+1}\\,j=-2\\,j \\\\ F(1,-2) & =\\frac{-2}{(1)(-2)+1}\\,i+\\frac{1}{(1)(-2)+1}\\,j=2\\,i-j \\\\ F(0,2) & =\\frac{2}{(0)(2)+1}\\,i+\\frac{0}{(0)(2)+1}\\,j=2\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/8e/8ec9af02a374c1b8a954117ad055f78e9e2ac74bc391bb230968198a3a474fef.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387284 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9a9e026-4bc7-575e-be23-f281b7660b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d688cdc804635688df6780bfb674622a491528c85802397cc3dccb6bd4a2d6be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387286} {:answer/id #uuid "60880678-2b0d-57f7-8c8d-ae95a3c4b0f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1f/1f597a7886abe6a8cddca9192658c8ded57dd96b010dfbf166e8cea6484872e7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387287} {:answer/id #uuid "71e0ba0c-ade1-5e87-9ac1-d66c6f763265" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/11/114f65bec341c3bef23ffda186b7d5a721e89e607d15c64624b6145e734c68c0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387288} {:answer/id #uuid "4150b677-4ab5-5642-97f3-e462d77d1b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8b/8b20800589467fa460547519312ed283d373ce2b7553b0c397413799b2d6597f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387289} {:answer/id #uuid "bcafb174-7327-5bc3-a3a6-55a1c3530cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/5317b575c101e4a782e17f9f83f56f66f8151a1d1c12cd0084020429435ba542.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9a9e026-4bc7-575e-be23-f281b7660b3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d688cdc804635688df6780bfb674622a491528c85802397cc3dccb6bd4a2d6be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387286} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7e4ea8-2187-5984-93cd-b8162a3b3097" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387285}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "709ee56e-badf-53e5-8fe9-cd6e97119ca1" :question/math-academy-id "q-122752" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=(y-2x)\\,i+(2y-4x)\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,3),(-1,-1),$ and $(3,2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=(y-2x)\\,i+(2y-4x)\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,3) & =(3-2(1))\\,i+(2(3)-4(1))\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ F(-1,-1) & =(-1-2(-1))\\,i+(2(-1)-4(-1))\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ F(3,2) & =(2-2(3))\\,i+(2(2)-4(3))\\,j=-4\\,i-8\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/d6/d688cdc804635688df6780bfb674622a491528c85802397cc3dccb6bd4a2d6be.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d40339cb-9f8c-56b1-9446-2bb79c2ae322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c9fc6ae3cbbf6fa3d241d3607b26fee1cd0670fde37494638ca90da2b02ecfa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387293} {:answer/id #uuid "3b36441e-f03d-5f2c-b78a-49b57116a3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387294} {:answer/id #uuid "116d6c88-d5ff-5163-b1bc-a148e6194baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e9efea8998b1dbaab3cc6d89dce4f99bdb06066e81fcb78a2b3a0e412e2e44c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387295} {:answer/id #uuid "e73588d4-0678-5e1c-aac4-ffad61b46f23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/80/80ecb3a560bc23359c3b44baace0523bfe653f0c5a5fee5b5c646d901ade5feb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387296} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c0c612-25c2-5765-8c88-fa1c6a482813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/040d62d956945b7bb67cae560cda4e09a22be2fa9cd2e5da3f3cc372269f14e4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b36441e-f03d-5f2c-b78a-49b57116a3cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387294} :answer-field/id #uuid "c92e3f54-7df7-528f-9e7f-fbd995c31ee0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387292}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b5b3650-421e-53e6-b6b4-9b4c7a243072" :question/math-academy-id "q-122754" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=(y-2)\\,i+(x+2)\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-5,3),(0,0),$ and $(2,-3).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=(y-2)\\,i+(x+2)\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(-5,3) & =(3-2)\\,i+(-5+2)\\,j=i-3\\,j \\\\ F(0,0) & =(0-2)\\,i+(0+2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(2,-3) & =(-3-2)\\,i+(2+2)\\,j=-5\\,i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/d6/d6084f0711f728a09a78c9803bec9c6e54274d6d72a2adc2b1547651e0ec702c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e846d3-cfa4-53b9-966f-e4adab0cb729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d502f64bd89571fcd7ccb43e339b0fb8554ebf2072d48eaf10829f96f9c170e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417331} {:answer/id #uuid "acf72fee-ab09-5c2f-a567-2d99703c6cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eac1fe8c8dee7394a49603187829adcc0fa81665e0eafb2674f43ebdf4493f10.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417334} {:answer/id #uuid "b10e879c-3c4a-5dd0-9361-bbc17fe37c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5d/5d27f4544c601da995ad2c1402547a477a244a6b79bff4e8b79f945299b73b87.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417335} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5ff7a9-5c75-54e7-82a4-5ae809e4f3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e40599ebb674fe5fe05c60be75f148f41458469ae6926c3388675ecdb24f66cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417337} {:answer/id #uuid "d640a56e-f8d2-517d-a8ab-e60c9f56c036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59bf689a32a8a0c5d347f29065acea60194b9f4b0fad084108ecb657257cd939.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf5ff7a9-5c75-54e7-82a4-5ae809e4f3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e40599ebb674fe5fe05c60be75f148f41458469ae6926c3388675ecdb24f66cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417337} :answer-field/id #uuid "b10e9eb4-ee70-5020-8593-2fc167326803" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417341}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d04f0b91-140d-549f-8f9d-31d1d9b6c7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122758" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the vector field $F(x,y)=-x\\,i-y\\,j$ at the indicated points?" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,4),(2,-2),$ and $(4,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the function $F(x,y)=-x\\,i-y\\,j\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1,4) & =-(1)\\,i-4\\,j=-i-4\\,j \\\\ F(2,-2) & =-(2)\\,i-(-2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ F(4,-2) & =-(4)\\,i-(-2)\\,j=-4\\,i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now draw our vectors. At each point, we draw the vector associated with that point, placing the tail end of the vector on the point itself. This gives the following diagram.\n\n![](images/e4/e40599ebb674fe5fe05c60be75f148f41458469ae6926c3388675ecdb24f66cf.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172084 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171890 :question/id #uuid "8f9615ef-b53e-51ee-9aa6-4df88afd6773" :question/math-academy-id "e-9441" :question/problem "![](images/29/2966d95bee0326ed5bf5a5fec9313d15bacd86334f9e9d144ff366bee63d9de3.png)\n\n \n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?\n\n- $\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}$\n\n- $\\mathbf G(x,y) = 2 \\, \\mathbf{i}$\n\n- $\\mathbf H(x,y) = -x \\, \\mathbf{i}$" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $\\mathbf j$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(x,y) = \\mathbf{i} + \\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' horizontal components (i.e., the $\\mathbf i$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf G(x,y) = 2 \\, \\mathbf{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $\\mathbf{H}(x,y) = -x\\, \\mathbf{i}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9734fc0-9789-5a9c-8ae0-806f87052875" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9798dcb4-1378-51aa-94b5-6f2b05c5a513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x, y) = xi - j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168520} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ab7585-cdb1-5031-b00c-6bd7293fb822" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x, y) = i + 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168521} {:answer/id #uuid "74fe15fc-2329-5341-9f1b-ca6399a41099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x, y) =-xi + yj" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168522} {:answer/id #uuid "77138ede-65f3-5aa8-859e-7ba94c5edf9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168523} {:answer/id #uuid "79114562-ae7e-51b9-8192-e814accd7704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x, y) = i - 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168524}] :answer-field/id #uuid "69c09b2e-0e0e-5814-9b8e-43892aa92ebf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168519}] :question/id #uuid "561ee574-102b-5192-93c3-2aebaaee05b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-122296" :question/problem "![](images/14/14a67562652c609deeaf6b7606cee130685e2c2b5382f1a5436cd4e441591b94.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172277 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05602332-e37c-5460-b172-b751e231ce9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253707} {:answer/id #uuid "22a9c2bb-60e1-58e5-9874-7cbd061245fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253982} {:answer/id #uuid "975ec189-e7bf-53b5-bbdd-1f4be9ecf1b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255004} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d17860-5ab2-534f-9821-dacba55fba0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255244} {:answer/id #uuid "c9697585-eb9c-571c-9a60-d1c3239f7491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22a9c2bb-60e1-58e5-9874-7cbd061245fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253982} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff26018b-9fd9-5c42-b4cb-d605e4c4ebfe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b0d06ed-9894-556b-a427-a46e4623bd10" :question/math-academy-id "q-122463" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3614ea1954f36435eb1ab5f52c04d4fa3062ac337eccf76a5b47e4a03a64a1b.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i-2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=-i+j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0560a0e5-3c64-5c20-ba01-0f4c2befe53b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=2\\,i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253708} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1acef0-096e-5556-9f93-be14a82e5b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253907} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc6c128-ebca-5a8b-9698-2fa7cca63d7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254190} {:answer/id #uuid "5d0fc214-fc5a-5e41-9871-649ee0d5d24b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=i+x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254495} {:answer/id #uuid "a5376f4d-7b12-543b-a551-ae03955027c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=i+2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d0fc214-fc5a-5e41-9871-649ee0d5d24b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=i+x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254495} :answer-field/id #uuid "948987f7-66fc-57d2-8b1e-f9f08b7df17e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256193}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d79ce833-b5df-5f7a-a69b-3af96b3bd56d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122629" :question/problem "![](images/34/34aca579b2890586365298c764d051f57d4c80977ee975caad505c923343f90d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is positive for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=-i+x\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=i+2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=2\\,i-j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y)=i+x\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0feaf718-9c43-5258-8ff7-15b33841980d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253812} {:answer/id #uuid "240ad4bf-ad85-5774-8e63-d0fe2d0c5637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=-i+2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253994} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff572d8-afc6-5dba-b636-ebe15c35810d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=x\\,i-y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254365} {:answer/id #uuid "505958de-9427-5e52-8d6c-57dee92e3f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254369} {:answer/id #uuid "5a33bd05-aafe-5ca0-8291-65d2e919e162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "505958de-9427-5e52-8d6c-57dee92e3f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254369} :answer-field/id #uuid "31154f67-e955-5021-90d3-73fe1888a1b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256007}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01c701e2-d5c4-5318-a60e-f5d847761bce" :question/math-academy-id "q-122631" :question/problem "![](images/77/77f88ec1dfbd85b4609800484963d2480e68009eb4ac1f6c9fb620914633ff2a.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=-i+2\\,j,\\,H(x,y)=x\\,i-y\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nK(x,y)=-2\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $F(x,y)=-y\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba98b8c-2116-50e2-b2de-6aae7dbae22c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-i-2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254058} {:answer/id #uuid "735ac856-ee4b-5c8a-9daf-474103fa33a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254692} {:answer/id #uuid "a2214b75-4ff9-5986-b2e2-09f3f7eea2eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255100} {:answer/id #uuid "e51e621f-adf6-56d4-ba3a-23552d243dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255694} {:answer/id #uuid "fce86be7-59a1-5b1f-98d2-ae97d81427f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "735ac856-ee4b-5c8a-9daf-474103fa33a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=x\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254692} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1d0012-9007-5d62-a389-7be8930ea3d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256203}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b5e48f80-38d5-59fb-be5e-a4668cd85716" :question/math-academy-id "q-122632" :question/problem "![](images/a0/a032eb49f78ce7bd54de6969f030e4316f2bd3028280f73991af3fe45521733c.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=i+j,\\,K(x,y)=-i-2\\,j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the horizontal direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=5\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=x\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256682 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1594a1bc-f5fe-5f70-9851-0a40cf220726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=y\\,i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253858} {:answer/id #uuid "2a58e0ad-829d-534a-8952-ebde58ad8036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=x\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254047} {:answer/id #uuid "806ab92f-6629-5c21-bfaa-aed813f56f31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=y\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254806} {:answer/id #uuid "a3040035-3b3f-530d-ab79-811b4208c92b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255108} {:answer/id #uuid "c489f169-2513-54a3-8d41-2efa377862b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "806ab92f-6629-5c21-bfaa-aed813f56f31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=y\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254806} :answer-field/id #uuid "7217108e-c492-5bb5-ac37-d69d40646a57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256127}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de025ac4-8073-535b-a254-6c2938769096" :question/math-academy-id "q-122633" :question/problem "![](images/25/251e49513353092b4f9a16f54bb14fbaa1afe1a14e5fecf5b3ce54905fed474d.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is zero for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=y\\,i+j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' horizontal components (i.e., the $i$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=x\\,i,\\,K(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $G(x,y)=y\\,i.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256683 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76b802a1-bd57-507e-9d5f-2fc8163a8ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254720} {:answer/id #uuid "a032e651-0cf8-5329-91d1-1c3f7ceb5a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255082} {:answer/id #uuid "a7435040-9bd5-51fd-be96-decf4409f227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255149} {:answer/id #uuid "c0557434-e79c-58c5-a3d7-f32cbf4b4359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255381} {:answer/id #uuid "e02a5494-bc39-5aa0-84ae-eb5ee949e1e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76b802a1-bd57-507e-9d5f-2fc8163a8ec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254720} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff28f4c7-b721-56cb-a6ef-a2b3a670e104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256368}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4eb6b577-c2ea-57ca-93b4-a6dc4a523e65" :question/math-academy-id "q-122634" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d13f8c3fdea65c5f05df12585aec7e18564bdbe390ebb895b8b2d01dda74708a.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is zero for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=j,\\,F(x,y)=-j\n$$\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is positive for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nH(x,y)=-i\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $K(x,y)=i.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1841502c-c704-5a4b-94ce-aa056d8b2d8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=-3\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253879} {:answer/id #uuid "726b2edc-7b83-5828-8edf-c66b8e7d2498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=2\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254684} {:answer/id #uuid "a86f4809-c346-50e5-bed8-9083aa709ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255154} {:answer/id #uuid "ba5823e1-ac01-5c74-ae2d-cf1e431ff2ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=4\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255330} {:answer/id #uuid "f25fec05-4300-51c1-8fa4-4555e55ebdab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f25fec05-4300-51c1-8fa4-4555e55ebdab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-5\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255789} :answer-field/id #uuid "3803374d-ed66-5409-8623-1564a0c2ca2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256020}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6a55635-2f53-567e-bc46-3d92630e23fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-122637" :question/problem "![](images/72/721252c30370d98fe776ca00e43fef9c95a5a074140dfbdf2a00be19a66b4a1e.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is zero for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=4\\,i,\\,K(x,y)=-3\\,i\n$$\n\n- The vertical component (i.e., the $j$ component) is negative for each vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=2\\,j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=-5\\,j.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4da5c52-6b5c-54df-b17f-83bd497bbf4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "K(x,y)=x\\,i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380652} {:answer/id #uuid "b86e90fc-a436-523b-9da9-b9d702be5d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-2\\,i+y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380653} {:answer/id #uuid "4def1406-b9da-59de-bc30-2b42c0b648cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380654} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd94f63-83b8-5cbf-89e4-6e021e2d4702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "G(x,y)=i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380655} {:answer/id #uuid "de1c9265-3201-5314-9c89-061c3e096082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "F(x,y)=-i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b86e90fc-a436-523b-9da9-b9d702be5d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "H(x,y)=-2\\,i+y\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380653} :answer-field/id #uuid "37acc21f-bf89-54d6-b6f6-f05fa5abc515" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186380651}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74301975-54ad-5b09-8f34-be154a2d8d2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122630" :question/problem "![](images/51/51ee68a4b95a815cc9372c4d6c1b739464de223375fa301d4cf3cdb1e6e5e829.png)\n\nWhich of the following could be the function that generates the vector field above?" :question/worked-solution "We notice the following:\n\n- The horizontal component (i.e., the $i$ component) is negative for *every* vector in our vector field. Therefore, we can rule out the following options:\n\n$$\nG(x,y)=i+j,\\,K(x,y)=x\\,i+j\n$$\n\n- As we move away from the origin in the vertical direction, our vectors' vertical components (i.e., the $j$ components) get longer. Therefore, we can rule out the following option:\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=-i+j\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the diagram corresponds to the vector field $H(x,y)=-2\\,i+y\\,j.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Two-Dimensional Vector Field"}]}
